experiment: blockfloor
  instrument        blockfloor   trial seed 0000000001352cd9   2000 trials
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  question          `compartprobe` refuted BOTH reasons `mask-unaffordable`
                    gave for its 59%: silencing the blocked neurons recovers
                    nothing, and blocking twice as many costs no more. What
                    is left is a cost that is ALL-OR-NOTHING, with no account.
  the cheap test    every width ever measured has been LARGE -- 25/50/75%.
                    Nobody has blocked ONE neuron. If one costs what four
                    costs, the cost is in the MECHANISM, not the larynx.
  the precedent     `set_reward_mask` once ALLOWED its range and froze the
                    whole network, and produced a flat curve for an entire
                    run before anyone noticed. Flat curves have earned this.
  the F1 group      14 neurons of vocal's 126. A "quarter blocked" is FOUR
                    CELLS, and a centroid over ten survivors instead of
                    fourteen is coarser than the fraction makes it sound.
  the anchor        `b4` must reproduce ~57%. If it does not, this run
                    disagrees with the one that just produced that number on
                    the same genome and code, and THAT outranks the curve.
